
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stretching & Flexibility | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  description="Explore daily stretching routines, flexibility exercises, mobility, posture, warm-ups, and cool-down techniques."
  heroTitle="Stretching & Flexibility"
  heroText="Improve mobility, encourage comfortable movement, and make stretching part of your everyday wellness routine."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Fitness & Active Living</p>
    <h1>Stretching, Flexibility & Mobility</h1>
    <p>
      Stretching is a simple way to include mindful movement
      in your daily routine. From gentle morning stretches
      to post-workout cool-downs, explore practical ways
      to develop flexibility, mobility, and comfortable
      movement throughout the day.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stretch-intro">
    <h2>Why Stretching Matters</h2>
    <p>
      Flexibility exercises help maintain or improve the
      range of motion around your joints. Mobility work
      encourages controlled movement, while regular
      stretching can complement strength training,
      walking, and cardiovascular exercise. A consistent,
      comfortable routine is more valuable than forcing
      yourself into difficult positions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stretch-grid">
    <article class="stretch-card">
      <span class="stretch-number">01</span>
      <h2>Morning Stretching</h2>
      <p>
        A gentle morning routine can help you ease into
        the day with comfortable movements and a little
        time for yourself.
      </p>
      <h3>Morning Movements</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Gentle shoulder rolls.</li>
        <li>Standing side stretches.</li>
        <li>Slow upper-body rotations.</li>
        <li>Gentle calf stretches.</li>
        <li>Easy seated or standing stretches.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="stretch-card">
      <span class="stretch-number">02</span>
      <h2>Full-Body Stretching</h2>
      <p>
        A full-body routine can include the shoulders,
        back, hips, legs, and calves. Move slowly and
        stay within a comfortable range.
      </p>
      <h3>Areas to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Shoulder and chest stretches.</li>
        <li>Upper-back stretches.</li>
        <li>Gentle hip flexor stretches.</li>
        <li>Hamstring stretches.</li>
        <li>Calf and ankle stretches.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="stretch-card">
      <span class="stretch-number">03</span>
      <h2>Back & Posture</h2>
      <p>
        Gentle back and upper-body movements can help
        counter long periods of sitting and encourage
        awareness of posture.
      </p>
      <h3>Movements to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Seated upper-back rotations.</li>
        <li>Gentle chest-opening stretches.</li>
        <li>Shoulder blade squeezes.</li>
        <li>Cat-cow movements.</li>
        <li>Gentle standing side bends.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="stretch-card">
      <span class="stretch-number">04</span>
      <h2>Hip & Leg Flexibility</h2>
      <p>
        The hips and legs are involved in everyday
        activities such as walking, climbing stairs,
        and getting up from a chair.
      </p>
      <h3>Stretching Ideas</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Seated hamstring stretches.</li>
        <li>Standing quadriceps stretches with support.</li>
        <li>Gentle hip flexor stretches.</li>
        <li>Figure-four stretches.</li>
        <li>Calf stretches against a wall.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="stretch-card">
      <span class="stretch-number">05</span>
      <h2>Mobility & Joint Movement</h2>
      <p>
        Mobility exercises focus on controlled movement
        through a comfortable range of motion. They can
        be included before exercise or during daily breaks.
      </p>
      <h3>Mobility Exercises</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Gentle ankle circles.</li>
        <li>Shoulder circles.</li>
        <li>Controlled hip circles.</li>
        <li>Gentle seated spinal rotations.</li>
        <li>Wrist and hand movements.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="stretch-card">
      <span class="stretch-number">06</span>
      <h2>Warm-Ups & Cool-Downs</h2>
      <p>
        Warm-ups prepare you for activity with gradual
        movement. Cool-downs allow you to slow down
        after exercise and finish with gentle stretching.
      </p>
      <h3>Routine Ideas</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Begin with a few minutes of easy walking.</li>
        <li>Include gentle arm and leg movements.</li>
        <li>Gradually increase activity intensity.</li>
        <li>Slow your pace after exercise.</li>
        <li>Finish with comfortable static stretches.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="stretch-routine">
    <p class="eyebrow">Everyday Wellness</p>
    <h2>A Simple Daily Stretching Routine</h2>
    <p>
      This sample routine offers a gentle way to include
      stretching throughout the day. Adapt the movements
      and duration to your comfort and experience.
    </p>

    <div class="stretch-table">
      <div class="stretch-row">
        <strong>Morning</strong>
        <span>Gentle shoulder, back, and leg stretches</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stretch-row">
        <strong>Midday</strong>
        <span>Short movement break and posture reset</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stretch-row">
        <strong>Before Exercise</strong>
        <span>Easy walking and dynamic movements</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stretch-row">
        <strong>After Exercise</strong>
        <span>Slow cool-down and comfortable static stretches</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stretch-row">
        <strong>Evening</strong>
        <span>Relaxed stretching and gentle mobility</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stretch-note">
    <h2>Stretch Comfortably & Consistently</h2>
    <p>
      Stretching should feel controlled and comfortable,
      never forced. Avoid bouncing or pushing into pain.
      Breathe naturally, move slowly, and give your body
      time to adapt. If you have an injury, persistent
      discomfort, or a medical condition that affects
      movement, seek guidance from an appropriate health
      professional before beginning a new routine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stretch-links">
    <h2>Explore More Fitness Activities</h2>
    <div class="stretch-link-grid">
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/">Workouts & Exercise Routines →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/walking/">Walking & Cardio →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/low-impact/">Low-Impact Exercise →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/recovery/">Recovery & Rest →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="stretch-back">
    <a href="/fitness/">← Return to Fitness</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .stretch-intro {
    margin: 30px 0;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .stretch-intro h2,
  .stretch-routine h2,
  .stretch-note h2,
  .stretch-links h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .stretch-intro p,
  .stretch-routine > p:not(.eyebrow),
  .stretch-note p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .stretch-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 35px 0;
  }

  .stretch-card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .stretch-number {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .stretch-card h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 13px;
  }

  .stretch-card h3 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }

  .stretch-card p,
  .stretch-card li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .stretch-card p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .stretch-card ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .stretch-routine {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .stretch-routine .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .stretch-table {
    margin-top: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .stretch-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr;
    gap: 15px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .stretch-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .stretch-row strong {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
  }

  .stretch-row span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .stretch-note {
    padding: 30px;
    margin: 40px 0;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .stretch-links {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .stretch-link-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 15px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .stretch-link-grid a {
    display: block;
    padding: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .stretch-link-grid a:hover {
    background: var(--rose-wash);
  }

  .stretch-back {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .stretch-back a {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .stretch-back a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .stretch-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .stretch-link-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .stretch-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 5px;
    }
  }
</style>
